<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Direct LinkML representation of prov:Entity. Applied to physical, digital, conceptual, and assertion-bearing things that participate in provenance relations. PROVENANCE SCOPE (alpha.5 design decision): for classes whose instances are real-world referents (structures, deities, places, actors), the provenance slots (was_derived_from, was_attributed_to, was_generated_by, generated_at_time) describe the DATA RECORD about the referent, not the referent itself -- a stupa is not generated by the survey that records it. Referent-level history is modelled through events (Production, DestructionEvent, etc.). RDF deployments SHOULD carry record-level provenance in named graphs or on InformationObject/Assertion nodes."@en .
